WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:11.291
[train whistle blaring]

2
00:00:16.208 --> 00:00:17.833
[Triste] It's too much for me. You try.

3
00:00:17.916 --> 00:00:19.583
[José Arcadio II]
It's impossible like that.

4
00:00:19.666 --> 00:00:21.333
- [Triste] Come on.
- It's impossible.

5
00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:26.791
- Good night.
- See you soon. cousin.

6
00:00:27.291 --> 00:00:30.041
- I'll let you win next time. all right?
- And gotta practice.

7
00:00:33.916 --> 00:00:34.750
Hello.

8
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:37.583
Hey.

9
00:00:37.666 --> 00:00:39.666
[unsettling music playing]

10
00:00:47.916 --> 00:00:49.000
[man] Aureliano.

11
00:01:00.833 --> 00:01:02.250
[man] Aureliano.

12
00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:04.291
- [gunshot]
- No!

13
00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:06.416
[woman breathes shakily]

14
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.291
[sobs] No!

15
00:01:12.375 --> 00:01:13.375
[man] Aureliano.

16
00:01:15.083 --> 00:01:16.416
- [gunshot]
- [clucking]

17
00:01:17.666 --> 00:01:18.500
[bell tolls]

18
00:01:18.583 --> 00:01:19.666
Aureliano.

19
00:01:37.208 --> 00:01:38.291
[music fades]

20
00:01:38.375 --> 00:01:40.708
[narrator] <i>Over the course</i>
<i>of a single week.</i>

21
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.958
<i>all 17 Aurelianos</i>
<i>were hunted down like rabbits</i>

22
00:01:45.041 --> 00:01:48.041
<i>by invisible criminals… who killed them.</i>

23
00:01:48.125 --> 00:01:51.333
<i>taking aim at the ash crosses</i>
<i>on their foreheads.</i>

24
00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:53.416
[melancholy music playing]

25
00:01:55.375 --> 00:01:57.375
[footsteps approaching]

26
00:02:02.416 --> 00:02:04.416
Those bastards got to Centeno too.

27
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.625
[Úrsula] My God.

28
00:02:09.375 --> 00:02:10.791
Who could have done this?

29
00:02:13.708 --> 00:02:15.875
[José Arcadio II]
No one in Macondo saw anything.

30
00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:18.500
There are no witnesses anywhere.

31
00:02:20.416 --> 00:02:21.750
[Aureliano] Witnesses?

32
00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:25.791
Are you serious. José Arcadio?

33
00:02:28.583 --> 00:02:31.458
You're telling me
you need someone to confirm

34
00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:35.250
that your bosses did this
with the help of the government?

35
00:02:35.333 --> 00:02:36.166
No.

36
00:02:37.458 --> 00:02:40.541
[Aureliano] Who branded their foreheads
like they were cattle?

37
00:02:41.625 --> 00:02:42.500
Hmm?

38
00:02:43.333 --> 00:02:44.250
Let's go.

39
00:02:44.875 --> 00:02:46.000
[Aureliano] Gerineldo.

40
00:02:47.291 --> 00:02:50.791
We're going to show
those gringo motherfuckers

41
00:02:51.875 --> 00:02:54.583
that they are not the ones
in charge in Colombia.

42
00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.083
You understand?

43
00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:00.083
- Aureliano.
- Hmm?

44
00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:04.666
I knew age had caught up with you.
but not this much.

45
00:03:07.208 --> 00:03:10.250
I'm terribly sorry. my friend.
but someone had to say it.

46
00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:11.333
[Aureliano] Hmm.

47
00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:15.166
Grieving is the only thing left
for you to do now.

48
00:03:16.208 --> 00:03:17.250
[Aureliano] Mm-hmm.

49
00:03:19.625 --> 00:03:20.625
[grunts]

50
00:03:25.125 --> 00:03:26.250
[groans]

51
00:03:26.833 --> 00:03:28.833
[breathing heavily]

52
00:03:36.041 --> 00:03:39.750
If you've come here to defend them.
get the fuck out.

53
00:03:44.291 --> 00:03:46.875
I was the last person to see Triste alive.

54
00:03:49.666 --> 00:03:53.458
And I'm gonna keep asking questions
because someone's gotta pay for this.

55
00:03:54.416 --> 00:03:56.916
The only one who's paying here is me.

56
00:04:00.375 --> 00:04:02.458
And that's exactly what they want.

57
00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:04.541
[dark ethereal music playing]

58
00:04:09.125 --> 00:04:11.166
You know. maybe I deserved it.

59
00:04:13.583 --> 00:04:15.666
No one deserves to suffer like this.

60
00:04:24.916 --> 00:04:26.791
You never understood war.

61
00:04:30.041 --> 00:04:31.291
Leave me alone.

62
00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.666
Leave me alone.

63
00:04:38.458 --> 00:04:43.208
[narrator] <i>Just as during the war.</i>
<i>after the deaths of his dearest friends.</i>

64
00:04:43.708 --> 00:04:45.625
<i>the colonel felt no sorrow.</i>

65
00:04:46.375 --> 00:04:49.416
<i>but rather a blind and directionless rage.</i>

66
00:04:50.291 --> 00:04:52.375
<i>An exhausting helplessness.</i>

67
00:04:58.416 --> 00:04:59.750
<i>He was lost…</i>

68
00:05:02.166 --> 00:05:05.500
<i>adrift in a strange house</i>
<i>where nothing and no one</i>

69
00:05:05.583 --> 00:05:08.208
<i>evoked the slightest hint of affection.</i>

70
00:05:08.291 --> 00:05:09.916
[laughter echoes]

71
00:05:11.708 --> 00:05:14.125
[narrator] <i>The air was filled</i>
<i>with the unbearable stench</i>

72
00:05:14.208 --> 00:05:15.916
<i>of rotten memories.</i>

73
00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.500
[lively music plays]

74
00:05:23.458 --> 00:05:25.458
[dark ethereal music continues]

75
00:05:38.125 --> 00:05:41.541
[narrator] <i>It was on October 11th.</i>
<i>at ten minutes past four.</i>

76
00:05:41.625 --> 00:05:44.000
<i>that for the first time since his youth.</i>

77
00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:47.916
<i>the colonel knowingly stepped</i>
<i>into a trap of nostalgia…</i>

78
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.000
[elephant trumpets]

79
00:05:51.708 --> 00:05:56.833
<i>…as he relived the wondrous afternoon</i>
<i>when his father took him to discover ice.</i>

80
00:05:56.916 --> 00:05:58.916
[wistful music playing]

81
00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.083
[footsteps thumping]

82
00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:34.083
[elephant trumpets]

83
00:07:25.125 --> 00:07:27.125
[wistful music continues]

84
00:08:11.166 --> 00:08:13.166
[music fades]

85
00:08:24.958 --> 00:08:26.791
[narrator] <i>And when it was all over.</i>

86
00:08:27.833 --> 00:08:32.458
<i>he found himself face-to-face</i>
<i>with his miserable solitude once again.</i>

87
00:08:35.833 --> 00:08:40.791
<i>So he walked over to the chestnut tree.</i>
<i>with the circus still on his mind.</i>

88
00:08:40.875 --> 00:08:42.875
[melancholy music playing]

89
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.000
[urine splashing]

90
00:08:52.833 --> 00:08:53.833
Mm…

91
00:08:55.458 --> 00:08:59.041
[narrator] <i>He tried to keep thinking</i>
<i>about the circus while he urinated…</i>

92
00:09:02.458 --> 00:09:04.875
<i>but could no longer find memory of it.</i>

93
00:09:05.833 --> 00:09:08.250
[groaning]

94
00:09:16.083 --> 00:09:18.083
[grunts. groans]

95
00:09:22.375 --> 00:09:24.375
[melancholy music continues]

96
00:09:46.291 --> 00:09:48.291
[music fades]

97
00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.125
[Úrsula sniffles]

98
00:09:57.208 --> 00:09:59.208
[melancholy music resumes]

99
00:10:01.291 --> 00:10:04.000
You have found rest at last. my child.

100
00:10:04.875 --> 00:10:06.000
[sniffles]

101
00:10:11.208 --> 00:10:13.208
[Úrsula sobs]

102
00:10:36.416 --> 00:10:41.833
ONE HUNDRED YEARS OF SOLITUDE

103
00:10:46.583 --> 00:10:48.333
[indistinct chattering]

104
00:10:48.416 --> 00:10:52.375
[narrator] <i>Years later.</i>
<i>nobody in Macondo remembered the colonel.</i>

105
00:10:54.750 --> 00:11:00.333
IN MEMORY OF COLONEL AURELIANO BUENDÍA
RELENTLESS DEFENDER OF FREEDOM AND JUSTICE

106
00:11:00.416 --> 00:11:03.666
HIS FIGHT FOR A SOVEREIGN NATION
WILL LIVE ON IN THE HEART OF HIS PEOPLE

107
00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:07.250
- [people clamoring]
- [mysterious music playing]

108
00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:23.875
[narrator] <i>Aureliano Segundo</i>
<i>had become fat. violet. and tortoise-like.</i>

109
00:11:24.375 --> 00:11:27.458
<i>the result of an appetite</i>
<i>comparable only to José Arcadio's</i>

110
00:11:27.541 --> 00:11:30.000
<i>when he returned</i>
<i>from his trip around the world.</i>

111
00:11:31.458 --> 00:11:35.625
<i>And he became the undefeated champion</i>
<i>of the absurd eating contests</i>

112
00:11:35.708 --> 00:11:39.625
<i>of endurance and gluttony.</i>
<i>held at Petra Cotes's house.</i>

113
00:11:40.375 --> 00:11:44.708
<i>Until one unfortunate Saturday</i>
<i>when Camila Sagastume showed up.</i>

114
00:11:53.625 --> 00:11:54.833
"Dearest Mother."

115
00:11:55.625 --> 00:11:57.833
"Nothing brings me more joy
than reading in your letters

116
00:11:57.916 --> 00:11:59.833
how happy you and Father are."

117
00:12:09.083 --> 00:12:12.083
[young Meme] <i>As for me.</i>
<i>I have wonderful news to share with you.</i>

118
00:12:12.958 --> 00:12:16.750
<i>My graduation as a clavichord soloist</i>
<i>is set for the end of this month…</i>

119
00:12:20.291 --> 00:12:22.041
[clamoring continues]

120
00:12:22.125 --> 00:12:26.416
<i>…so it won't be long</i>
<i>before I return to Macondo for good.</i>

121
00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:29.250
[clamoring continues]

122
00:12:34.583 --> 00:12:36.500
<i>And nothing thrills me more</i>
<i>than the thought of</i>

123
00:12:36.583 --> 00:12:38.125
<i>living with the family again.</i>

124
00:12:38.208 --> 00:12:40.458
[man] Come on. you can do it!

125
00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.666
[music fades]

126
00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.750
[Aureliano II groans]

127
00:12:58.833 --> 00:13:00.041
Fernanda.

128
00:13:01.583 --> 00:13:02.916
Fernanda.

129
00:13:03.625 --> 00:13:05.958
[young Meme] See you soon. your daughter.

130
00:13:06.041 --> 00:13:07.041
Renata.

131
00:13:07.125 --> 00:13:08.208
[door opens]

132
00:13:10.375 --> 00:13:12.375
[Aureliano II groaning]

133
00:13:15.708 --> 00:13:16.625
[man] That's it.

134
00:13:18.083 --> 00:13:19.458
[labored breathing]

135
00:13:21.375 --> 00:13:23.041
[man] Ms. Petra sent you this.

136
00:13:24.958 --> 00:13:27.541
- [softly] Aureliano.
- Yeah. yeah. yeah.

137
00:13:29.291 --> 00:13:30.291
Aureliano.

138
00:13:30.375 --> 00:13:32.041
[bell ringing]

139
00:13:32.708 --> 00:13:34.416
Yeah. yeah. yeah. yeah.

140
00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.166
Aureliano. don't do this.

141
00:13:36.666 --> 00:13:38.666
[somber music playing]

142
00:13:40.166 --> 00:13:42.166
[rooster crows]

143
00:13:48.666 --> 00:13:50.000
What happened?

144
00:13:52.958 --> 00:13:54.583
A miracle. Aureliano.

145
00:13:55.333 --> 00:13:59.375
God has given you the opportunity
to prove you can be an honorable man

146
00:13:59.458 --> 00:14:01.125
and to be with your family.

147
00:14:02.458 --> 00:14:05.750
Not only that.
but Renata's coming home soon.

148
00:14:09.333 --> 00:14:11.750
[bell rings]

149
00:14:11.833 --> 00:14:14.833
- [machete's slicing]
- [men's shouting indistinctly]

150
00:14:16.375 --> 00:14:18.375
[carriage approaching]

151
00:14:21.166 --> 00:14:23.166
[indistinct shouting continues]

152
00:14:36.458 --> 00:14:39.166
[José Arcadio II] Hey. guys!
These are ready to go.

153
00:14:40.291 --> 00:14:43.333
Get liquid from that barrel.
There's more coming. Come on. come on!

154
00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:44.958
Sir.

155
00:14:45.041 --> 00:14:46.708
- Take this. Come on.
- Okay.

156
00:14:47.208 --> 00:14:48.583
[grunts] You got it.

157
00:14:48.666 --> 00:14:51.250
[man] Spray the ones over there
so we can get this done sooner.

158
00:14:52.541 --> 00:14:54.333
Here you go. That's it.

159
00:14:58.791 --> 00:14:59.875
Hey. give me a hand.

160
00:15:00.541 --> 00:15:02.166
Let's go. let's go. let's go!

161
00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.500
Come on. fellas. come on!

162
00:15:04.583 --> 00:15:05.416
[man] Here.

163
00:15:05.958 --> 00:15:07.083
What is that thing?

164
00:15:07.583 --> 00:15:09.958
It's a chemical they sent
to help save our crops.

165
00:15:10.458 --> 00:15:13.041
We have to kill the bugs
that are ruining our bananas.

166
00:15:13.666 --> 00:15:15.291
[narrator] <i>Lorenzo Gavilán.</i>

167
00:15:15.375 --> 00:15:18.750
<i>a colonel of the Mexican Revolution</i>
<i>exiled in Macondo.</i>

168
00:15:18.833 --> 00:15:23.083
<i>who claimed to have witnessed</i>
<i>the heroism of his comrade. Artemio Cruz.</i>

169
00:15:23.166 --> 00:15:26.250
<i>had come. like many others.</i>
<i>to work on the banana plantation.</i>

170
00:15:26.333 --> 00:15:28.000
One last thing. José Arcadio.

171
00:15:28.083 --> 00:15:29.750
What. Gavilán. what?

172
00:15:31.416 --> 00:15:35.333
The toilet they brought at Christmas…
is falling apart.

173
00:15:36.333 --> 00:15:39.041
It might be the latest Yankee invention.
but over here.

174
00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:44.083
we need some efficient
and dignified latrines. don't you think?

175
00:15:47.416 --> 00:15:49.291
- I'll talk to Mr. Brown.
- [train whistle blaring]

176
00:15:49.375 --> 00:15:51.375
[indistinct chattering]

177
00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:56.958
[street vendor] Empanadas! Fresh and hot!

178
00:15:59.291 --> 00:16:00.833
[man] It's the last train to town.

179
00:16:03.166 --> 00:16:05.166
[train whistle blaring]

180
00:16:14.416 --> 00:16:16.291
[conductor] Macondo!

181
00:16:17.083 --> 00:16:18.583
Macondo!

182
00:16:18.666 --> 00:16:21.333
Next stop. Fundación!

183
00:16:23.791 --> 00:16:26.125
Next stop. Fundación!

184
00:16:26.208 --> 00:16:27.166
[whistle blows]

185
00:16:27.666 --> 00:16:30.500
[conductor] Train leaves for Fundación
in ten minutes!

186
00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:33.458
[both laughing]

187
00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:40.875
Your mother doesn't get a hello?

188
00:16:44.166 --> 00:16:46.208
Mother Superior sends her best.

189
00:16:51.583 --> 00:16:53.291
When did my girl get so big. huh?

190
00:16:53.375 --> 00:16:54.250
[laughs]

191
00:16:54.333 --> 00:16:56.125
- Well. right back at ya!
- [both laugh]

192
00:16:56.208 --> 00:16:57.125
Renata!

193
00:16:58.041 --> 00:17:01.166
Come on. let's go home now.
Welcome home. sweetheart.

194
00:17:01.708 --> 00:17:02.833
You look beautiful.

195
00:17:03.333 --> 00:17:04.875
- Beautiful.
- You too. Papa.

196
00:17:04.958 --> 00:17:06.791
[both laughing]

197
00:17:06.875 --> 00:17:09.666
Mama Úrsula asks me every day.
"How's Meme?"

198
00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:11.250
- "How's Mem--"
- Aureliano Buendía.

199
00:17:11.333 --> 00:17:12.333
Mr. Brown.

200
00:17:13.666 --> 00:17:16.583
Coming back from. uh. the capital?
I didn't see you in first class.

201
00:17:17.291 --> 00:17:19.416
Mm. no. It was just my daughter. Meme.

202
00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:20.750
Uh. Renata.

203
00:17:20.833 --> 00:17:24.333
Well. pleased to meet you. señorita.
This is my daughter. Patricia.

204
00:17:24.416 --> 00:17:26.083
Nice to meet you. I'm Meme.

205
00:17:28.708 --> 00:17:30.041
Be polite.

206
00:17:30.125 --> 00:17:30.958
Hi.

207
00:17:32.208 --> 00:17:34.041
[Mr. Brown]
Visiting family in the capital?

208
00:17:34.125 --> 00:17:36.000
No. She was studying.

209
00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:39.291
My daughter is one of
the best clavichordists in the country.

210
00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:41.666
[Patricia chuckles]

211
00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:46.416
Well. why don't you come and play for us
at the company club sometime?

212
00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.375
- We'd be delighted to have you.
- Sure.

213
00:17:48.458 --> 00:17:50.125
- She'd love--
- We'll have to think about it.

214
00:17:50.625 --> 00:17:52.958
If you'll please excuse us.
we're expected for lunch.

215
00:17:53.583 --> 00:17:54.708
Mr. Brown.

216
00:17:54.791 --> 00:17:55.958
Señorita.

217
00:17:56.041 --> 00:17:57.083
[Mr. Brown] Goodbye.

218
00:17:57.583 --> 00:17:59.875
- Nice to meet you!
- Renata.

219
00:17:59.958 --> 00:18:00.833
That's enough.

220
00:18:00.916 --> 00:18:02.916
[melodic clavichord music playing]

221
00:18:07.333 --> 00:18:10.375
[narrator] <i>Although Meme hadn't really</i>
<i>found her true vocation.</i>

222
00:18:10.458 --> 00:18:12.416
<i>she had still earned the highest grades…</i>

223
00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:15.666
Give us this day our daily bread
and forgive us our trespasses.

224
00:18:15.750 --> 00:18:18.541
as we forgive those
who trespass against us.

225
00:18:18.625 --> 00:18:22.708
<i>…largely due to her unwavering discipline</i>
<i>to avoid upsetting her mother.</i>

226
00:18:22.791 --> 00:18:25.208
Our Father. who art in heaven.
hallowed be thy name.

227
00:18:25.291 --> 00:18:27.166
Thy kingdom come.

228
00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:29.458
Thy will be done on earth
as it is in heaven.

229
00:18:29.541 --> 00:18:31.041
[Aureliano II snoring]

230
00:18:32.583 --> 00:18:33.750
[snorts]

231
00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:41.250
[snoring continues]

232
00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:48.125
[narrator] <i>She endured performances</i>
<i>with the same stoicism</i>

233
00:18:48.208 --> 00:18:50.666
<i>with which she devoted herself</i>
<i>to her studies.</i>

234
00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:52.166
[music stops]

235
00:18:54.791 --> 00:18:56.708
[narrator] <i>That was the price</i>
<i>of her freedom.</i>

236
00:18:57.625 --> 00:18:58.500
[door opens]

237
00:19:00.125 --> 00:19:01.083
[retches]

238
00:19:02.541 --> 00:19:04.000
[coughing]

239
00:19:08.166 --> 00:19:09.458
[Aureliano II] Are you all right?

240
00:19:11.458 --> 00:19:14.083
We have to cancel the recital
at the plantation.

241
00:19:21.416 --> 00:19:23.916
- Fernanda. we talked about this already.
- I said no. Aureliano.

242
00:19:24.416 --> 00:19:25.416
I said no.

243
00:19:30.541 --> 00:19:32.500
- I'm pregnant.
- Mm. Hmm?

244
00:19:32.583 --> 00:19:34.500
[intriguing music playing]

245
00:19:34.583 --> 00:19:35.750
I'm not leaving this bed.

246
00:19:35.833 --> 00:19:39.000
and you're not going to convince me
to let Renata go by herself.

247
00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:41.791
All you need to do. Fernanda.

248
00:19:41.875 --> 00:19:45.166
is bring this child into the Buendía home
safe and sound.

249
00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:46.625
I'll take care of Meme.

250
00:19:46.708 --> 00:19:47.666
Mama Úrsula!

251
00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:49.666
- Aurelia--
- I'm going to be a father!

252
00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.375
[retching]

253
00:19:53.083 --> 00:19:54.958
[coughs. vomits]

254
00:19:55.041 --> 00:19:57.041
[intriguing music continues]

255
00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:01.958
[Fernanda] Swear it on the Virgin.
Christ. and the Holy Spirit. Renata.

256
00:20:02.041 --> 00:20:04.125
Decency. modesty. fear of God.

257
00:20:04.208 --> 00:20:06.666
for Christ. the Virgin.
and the Holy Spirit.

258
00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:07.666
And what else?

259
00:20:08.208 --> 00:20:09.041
What else?

260
00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:12.666
I promise I'll be back
before it gets dark.

261
00:20:13.166 --> 00:20:14.500
By our Lord and Savior.

262
00:20:14.583 --> 00:20:15.458
Amen.

263
00:20:16.291 --> 00:20:18.083
That's enough. Fernanda.

264
00:20:18.583 --> 00:20:22.041
She'll be fine as long as
she doesn't come back a Protestant.

265
00:20:23.458 --> 00:20:25.583
Go on. child. You go and have fun.

266
00:20:25.666 --> 00:20:26.541
[both chuckle]

267
00:20:26.625 --> 00:20:28.166
Enjoy yourself.

268
00:20:36.833 --> 00:20:38.833
[train whistle blaring]

269
00:20:38.916 --> 00:20:40.916
[soothing music playing]

270
00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:03.333
[young Meme] Uncle.

271
00:21:04.416 --> 00:21:05.833
do you live here too?

272
00:21:07.625 --> 00:21:10.416
No. it's only company executives
and their families.

273
00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:11.791
They're all American.

274
00:21:16.291 --> 00:21:17.708
Are they your friends?

275
00:21:21.208 --> 00:21:23.541
I mean. Mr. Brown has been
very good to me.

276
00:21:28.041 --> 00:21:29.958
- This is where the recital's at?
- Uh-huh.

277
00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.250
[young Meme] Patricia!

278
00:21:47.166 --> 00:21:49.666
[Patricia in Spanish]
Your name was Renata. right?

279
00:21:50.166 --> 00:21:51.083
[in English] Meme.

280
00:21:51.583 --> 00:21:54.083
But hey. please don't feel like
you need to talk to me in Spanish

281
00:21:54.166 --> 00:21:55.125
'cause we're in Macondo.

282
00:21:55.208 --> 00:21:57.250
I. uh. I can speak English.

283
00:21:57.958 --> 00:22:00.750
Very well. Meme.
Did you bring your bathing suit?

284
00:22:03.375 --> 00:22:04.375
No.

285
00:22:05.833 --> 00:22:06.875
May I borrow one?

286
00:22:07.791 --> 00:22:09.000
Of course.

287
00:22:09.083 --> 00:22:10.375
Give her your bathing suit.

288
00:22:12.625 --> 00:22:13.458
Okay.

289
00:22:14.041 --> 00:22:14.875
Come on.

290
00:22:15.916 --> 00:22:18.375
[José Arcadio II] Hey!
Where should I put the clavichord?

291
00:22:18.458 --> 00:22:21.333
We have more staff
in the grand hall. José Arcadio.

292
00:22:21.416 --> 00:22:22.500
You know that!

293
00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:24.208
Meme!

294
00:22:24.875 --> 00:22:26.583
I'll pick you up later this evening!

295
00:22:26.666 --> 00:22:27.750
Okay!

296
00:22:27.833 --> 00:22:29.833
[jazz music playing]

297
00:22:40.666 --> 00:22:42.666
[jazz music continues]

298
00:22:48.375 --> 00:22:49.375
[Patricia] Meme.

299
00:23:14.458 --> 00:23:15.416
[chuckles]

300
00:23:21.541 --> 00:23:22.666
[music fades]

301
00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:25.750
[clavichord music playing]

302
00:23:42.958 --> 00:23:44.958
[dramatic note plays]

303
00:23:51.333 --> 00:23:53.333
[dramatic clavichord music playing]

304
00:24:05.791 --> 00:24:06.916
[music stops]

305
00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:08.416
She is excellent.

306
00:24:08.500 --> 00:24:10.791
[dramatic clavichord music resumes]

307
00:24:14.333 --> 00:24:15.791
[music stops]

308
00:24:16.416 --> 00:24:18.333
[all clapping]

309
00:24:29.875 --> 00:24:31.750
- [jazz music playing]
- [young Meme] Wait!

310
00:24:32.250 --> 00:24:33.208
Patricia.

311
00:24:38.833 --> 00:24:40.458
Patricia. No.

312
00:24:41.291 --> 00:24:43.291
[both laughing]

313
00:24:48.458 --> 00:24:49.708
[Patricia laughs]

314
00:24:50.541 --> 00:24:51.708
[groans]

315
00:24:51.791 --> 00:24:53.916
Where were you all this time?

316
00:24:54.000 --> 00:24:55.875
- In a convent.
- [laughs]

317
00:24:59.208 --> 00:25:01.000
[both laughing]

318
00:25:01.583 --> 00:25:03.250
Come on. there's something
I wanna show you.

319
00:25:03.333 --> 00:25:04.625
No.

320
00:25:05.166 --> 00:25:07.833
- Meme! Come on.
- No. my uncle will be here any second.

321
00:25:07.916 --> 00:25:10.750
Meme! Are you still a nun or what?

322
00:25:10.833 --> 00:25:13.125
I will take you home later.

323
00:25:14.250 --> 00:25:16.250
[both laughing]

324
00:25:19.625 --> 00:25:20.958
- [bottle shatters]
- [gasps]

325
00:25:21.041 --> 00:25:22.416
[both laughing]

326
00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:27.125
[Patricia] Sh.

327
00:25:31.166 --> 00:25:33.625
- [Patricia clears throat]
- [indistinct chattering]

328
00:25:35.875 --> 00:25:37.541
[Patricia] Is Néstor around?

329
00:25:37.625 --> 00:25:40.250
No. miss. I'm sorry.
I think he went out with your father.

330
00:25:42.333 --> 00:25:44.125
Let's go. Come on.

331
00:25:44.791 --> 00:25:46.291
[man] What exactly do you need?

332
00:25:46.833 --> 00:25:49.458
Hey. can you drive us
around the plantation?

333
00:25:49.541 --> 00:25:51.083
[intriguing music playing]

334
00:25:51.166 --> 00:25:53.875
[man 2] No. that's not gonna work.
This is the spare.

335
00:25:55.416 --> 00:25:57.666
[narrator] <i>His name</i>
<i>was Mauricio Babilonia.</i>

336
00:25:57.750 --> 00:25:58.583
You got the key?

337
00:25:58.666 --> 00:26:01.583
[narrator] <i>He was born and raised</i>
<i>in Macondo</i>

338
00:26:01.666 --> 00:26:05.541
<i>and was an apprentice mechanic</i>
<i>in the banana company's workshops.</i>

339
00:26:07.375 --> 00:26:08.875
Okay. Let's go.

340
00:26:13.875 --> 00:26:15.083
[music fades]

341
00:26:15.833 --> 00:26:16.750
Meme!

342
00:26:18.791 --> 00:26:20.791
[shouting. laughing]

343
00:26:25.708 --> 00:26:27.708
[Patricia continues shouting. laughing]

344
00:26:36.333 --> 00:26:37.416
Do you wanna learn?

345
00:26:38.416 --> 00:26:41.291
Yes. you have to. Meme. Pull over here.

346
00:26:41.375 --> 00:26:43.375
Stop. stop. stop. Stop!

347
00:26:44.291 --> 00:26:45.625
[young Meme] What do I do?

348
00:26:45.708 --> 00:26:47.291
[Mauricio] Don't let go until I tell you.

349
00:26:47.375 --> 00:26:49.291
Then you can start
releasing the pedal slowly.

350
00:26:49.375 --> 00:26:51.333
Then at the same time.
you gotta press that pedal

351
00:26:51.416 --> 00:26:52.500
with your other foot.

352
00:26:54.625 --> 00:26:55.625
You got that?

353
00:27:01.583 --> 00:27:02.416
Like a piano.

354
00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:04.000
[Mauricio chuckles]

355
00:27:05.375 --> 00:27:07.958
Yeah! Come on. you can do it.
Come on. come on!

356
00:27:08.041 --> 00:27:10.333
All right. well.
I've told you everything you need to know.

357
00:27:11.333 --> 00:27:12.458
So hit it. Come on.

358
00:27:13.125 --> 00:27:16.000
- All right! Come on! Come on. go!
- Go ahead. Miss Know-it-all.

359
00:27:22.541 --> 00:27:24.375
- [screams]
- Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!

360
00:27:24.458 --> 00:27:27.208
- Slowly! Hey! Hey!
- [laughing]

361
00:27:27.291 --> 00:27:29.250
[lively percussive music playing]

362
00:27:29.333 --> 00:27:31.875
Now press the pedal again.
Hey. step on the pedal.

363
00:27:31.958 --> 00:27:32.958
Uh-huh.

364
00:27:33.041 --> 00:27:34.291
Let go. let go!

365
00:27:34.958 --> 00:27:36.583
Meme! Slow down. woman! Jesus!

366
00:27:36.666 --> 00:27:38.083
[Patricia] Faster. faster. faster!

367
00:27:38.166 --> 00:27:39.791
[Mauricio] Hey. slow down!
Slow down. stop!

368
00:27:40.458 --> 00:27:42.583
[girls laughing]

369
00:27:45.291 --> 00:27:46.291
Slowly. slowly.

370
00:27:46.375 --> 00:27:47.333
Did I scare ya?

371
00:27:47.416 --> 00:27:48.958
Come on. I'm not scared.

372
00:27:49.875 --> 00:27:51.458
[Patricia] Come on. faster!

373
00:27:52.791 --> 00:27:54.750
[laughs. screams]

374
00:27:57.583 --> 00:27:59.125
[music stops]

375
00:28:00.041 --> 00:28:02.166
We gotta start earlier tomorrow.

376
00:28:02.666 --> 00:28:04.916
We didn't get through
all of today's batches.

377
00:28:06.291 --> 00:28:07.958
[indistinct chattering]

378
00:28:08.666 --> 00:28:10.750
- What's the matter with you?
- [man sighs]

379
00:28:10.833 --> 00:28:13.291
My whole entire body's itching. Here.

380
00:28:15.291 --> 00:28:17.791
It's this stuff
they're having us spray. boss.

381
00:28:20.958 --> 00:28:22.333
Anybody else itching?

382
00:28:22.416 --> 00:28:24.791
[man 2] Hey. boys. show him.

383
00:28:24.875 --> 00:28:26.166
[man 3] Yeah. me too. boss.

384
00:28:28.125 --> 00:28:29.000
Look.

385
00:28:32.583 --> 00:28:34.083
[Gavilán] It's not just us.

386
00:28:34.666 --> 00:28:37.416
The women and children
have also been getting sick.

387
00:28:37.500 --> 00:28:39.208
What did they say at the health center?

388
00:28:39.291 --> 00:28:41.166
- [somber music playing]
- [chuckles]

389
00:28:41.750 --> 00:28:43.291
[scoffs] "The health center."

390
00:28:49.916 --> 00:28:53.041
[narrator] <i>The company's physicians</i>
<i>never examined the sick.</i>

391
00:28:54.666 --> 00:28:58.208
<i>Instead. a nurse would place</i>
<i>vibrant-turquoise-colored pills</i>

392
00:28:58.291 --> 00:28:59.541
<i>on their tongues.</i>

393
00:28:59.625 --> 00:29:03.375
<i>regardless if they had malaria.</i>
<i>gonorrhea. or constipation.</i>

394
00:29:07.625 --> 00:29:09.791
<i>It was such a common treatment</i>

395
00:29:09.875 --> 00:29:13.250
<i>that children would stand in line</i>
<i>several times.</i>

396
00:29:13.333 --> 00:29:16.583
<i>And instead of swallowing them.</i>
<i>they'd take the pills home</i>

397
00:29:16.666 --> 00:29:19.500
<i>and use them as markers</i>
<i>in games of lottery.</i>

398
00:29:20.875 --> 00:29:21.708
Hey.

399
00:29:41.500 --> 00:29:44.875
[José Arcadio II] What do the doctors say
about us using the chemicals?

400
00:29:44.958 --> 00:29:46.416
[Gavilán] That it's not the cause.

401
00:29:53.500 --> 00:29:55.458
And what's the problem with the toilet?

402
00:29:57.500 --> 00:29:58.958
[distant coughing]

403
00:30:06.208 --> 00:30:08.916
[indistinct chattering]

404
00:30:12.208 --> 00:30:14.208
[flies buzzing]

405
00:30:15.041 --> 00:30:16.500
[coughing]

406
00:30:17.541 --> 00:30:20.166
It's not just the chemicals
that are making us sick. my friend.

407
00:30:20.750 --> 00:30:21.750
[coughs]

408
00:30:24.500 --> 00:30:25.916
[music stops]

409
00:30:43.458 --> 00:30:45.458
[jazz music playing in distance]

410
00:30:57.583 --> 00:30:58.791
[knocking at door]

411
00:31:00.708 --> 00:31:01.833
Good evening. Cesa.

412
00:31:01.916 --> 00:31:04.041
Good evening. José Arcadio.

413
00:31:05.208 --> 00:31:08.000
- How are you?
- I'm fine. How are you?

414
00:31:09.041 --> 00:31:10.666
I need to speak to Mr. Brown.

415
00:31:11.166 --> 00:31:14.750
[Cesa] I'll get him for you.
He's a little busy. Come in.

416
00:31:15.791 --> 00:31:17.791
[laughter]

417
00:31:17.875 --> 00:31:19.416
[indistinct chattering]

418
00:31:19.500 --> 00:31:21.666
[Cesa] Sir. you have a visitor.

419
00:31:24.625 --> 00:31:27.250
[Mr. Brown] Give me a moment. everybody.
I'll be right back.

420
00:31:27.333 --> 00:31:29.125
- José Arcadio.
- Mr. Brown.

421
00:31:29.208 --> 00:31:30.541
- Buenas noches.
- Evening. sir.

422
00:31:30.625 --> 00:31:34.541
Mm. My daughter. Patricia.
already took your niece home.

423
00:31:34.625 --> 00:31:36.041
She's very talented.

424
00:31:36.125 --> 00:31:37.750
Give my congratulations to your brother.

425
00:31:37.833 --> 00:31:39.375
Seriously. she was great.

426
00:31:39.458 --> 00:31:42.250
I appreciate that. Mr. Brown.
but that's not why I'm here.

427
00:31:42.750 --> 00:31:44.250
Not sure if you recall before you left.

428
00:31:44.333 --> 00:31:46.583
I mentioned us having to solve a problem
with the barracks.

429
00:31:46.666 --> 00:31:48.458
Sure. we'll talk about it tomorrow.
I'm busy.

430
00:31:48.541 --> 00:31:49.375
No.

431
00:31:50.708 --> 00:31:52.208
I need to speak to you right now.

432
00:31:59.541 --> 00:32:00.791
Right. what's the matter?

433
00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:04.333
Half of my day workers are sick
and bedridden.

434
00:32:04.875 --> 00:32:07.333
The living and working conditions
are terrible.

435
00:32:07.416 --> 00:32:09.208
Which is why we gave 'em a health center.

436
00:32:09.291 --> 00:32:10.333
One that doesn't work.

437
00:32:10.416 --> 00:32:13.291
And I'm sorry. sir. but those medics
are not qualified for the job.

438
00:32:13.916 --> 00:32:16.375
They can go
to Aracataca or Fundación. then.

439
00:32:16.458 --> 00:32:17.833
What's the big deal?

440
00:32:19.458 --> 00:32:22.416
Sure. but we also have a problem
with the toilet.

441
00:32:22.500 --> 00:32:24.541
- The whole thing.
- Enough. foreman.

442
00:32:26.500 --> 00:32:27.375
Tomorrow.

443
00:32:28.291 --> 00:32:30.375
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

444
00:32:31.166 --> 00:32:32.583
Sorry for the intrusion.

445
00:32:34.791 --> 00:32:36.583
[Mr. Brown in Spanish]
Another whiskey. please.

446
00:32:36.666 --> 00:32:38.583
[in English] How's everybody else doing
on drinks?

447
00:32:42.958 --> 00:32:44.958
[narrator] <i>Meme never forgot that day.</i>

448
00:32:46.791 --> 00:32:49.458
<i>She had spent exhilarating hours</i>
<i>with Patricia.</i>

449
00:32:49.541 --> 00:32:51.833
<i>shedding tears of laughter and fear.</i>

450
00:32:54.875 --> 00:32:56.625
<i>And beyond the crisis.</i>

451
00:32:57.875 --> 00:32:59.958
<i>she had found a strange kind of bravery</i>

452
00:33:00.041 --> 00:33:02.750
<i>she had once needed</i>
<i>to run away from school.</i>

453
00:33:11.250 --> 00:33:14.833
Meme. do you promise
you'll come back soon and visit me?

454
00:33:15.625 --> 00:33:17.916
I promise. but you gotta get out of here.

455
00:33:29.666 --> 00:33:31.666
[vehicle drives away]

456
00:33:42.666 --> 00:33:44.208
Who drove you home?

457
00:33:45.375 --> 00:33:46.916
Patricia and her driver.

458
00:33:48.583 --> 00:33:50.791
[whispers] I forbid you
from ever going back.

459
00:33:52.875 --> 00:33:54.000
But why?

460
00:33:55.541 --> 00:33:57.500
You will not speak to me
like that. Renata.

461
00:33:59.166 --> 00:34:00.125
In fact…

462
00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:03.833
you're forbidden
from leaving this house alone.

463
00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:06.000
Forbidden!

464
00:34:09.708 --> 00:34:10.833
[young Meme grunts]

465
00:34:12.000 --> 00:34:13.333
[young Meme crying]

466
00:34:18.541 --> 00:34:20.708
It's just your mom's pregnancy.

467
00:34:21.791 --> 00:34:23.458
That's why she's like this.

468
00:34:25.291 --> 00:34:27.291
[Meme continues crying]

469
00:34:28.583 --> 00:34:30.916
How about a picture this weekend.
you and me?

470
00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:33.000
[footsteps approaching]

471
00:34:37.833 --> 00:34:39.875
You'd really take me to the pictures?

472
00:34:45.333 --> 00:34:46.333
[Meme sniffles]

473
00:34:47.625 --> 00:34:50.083
[in Spanish]
<i>♪ But he didn't invite the toad ♪</i>

474
00:34:50.166 --> 00:34:53.208
<i>♪ Because he told everything ♪</i>

475
00:34:53.291 --> 00:34:56.750
<i>♪ I saw the cat with the pig ♪</i>

476
00:34:56.833 --> 00:34:59.333
<i>♪ The dog. the rooster. and the cat ♪</i>

477
00:34:59.416 --> 00:35:04.458
<i>♪ Talking for a long time</i>
<i>In fluent Italian ♪</i>

478
00:35:04.958 --> 00:35:09.458
<i>♪ I saw the chick and his brother</i>
<i>Speaking German ♪</i>

479
00:35:09.541 --> 00:35:13.833
<i>♪ And I saw the hawk</i>
<i>Acting all high and mighty ♪</i>

480
00:35:13.916 --> 00:35:19.375
<i>♪ Invite them in Chinese</i>
<i>To buy soda and bread ♪</i>

481
00:35:19.458 --> 00:35:23.833
<i>♪ The day the cockroach</i>
<i>Fell in love with the centipede ♪</i>

482
00:35:23.916 --> 00:35:27.708
<i>♪ The butterfly shouted</i>
<i>She's crazy. she's drunk ♪</i>

483
00:35:28.208 --> 00:35:31.208
<i>♪ She's a spotless female ♪</i>

484
00:35:31.291 --> 00:35:33.625
<i>♪ She said with her face down ♪</i>

485
00:35:34.125 --> 00:35:39.250
<i>♪ He'll never work</i>
<i>Shouted the cricket loudly ♪</i>

486
00:35:39.791 --> 00:35:42.916
<i>♪ Because he's a simple guy ♪</i>

487
00:35:43.000 --> 00:35:46.416
<i>♪ And doesn't like disorder ♪</i>

488
00:35:47.333 --> 00:35:50.250
[in English] You have a glow about you
since your daughter returned.

489
00:36:00.833 --> 00:36:03.000
I was afraid that you'd be mad at me.

490
00:36:03.791 --> 00:36:06.500
[chuckles] Why would I be mad?

491
00:36:07.250 --> 00:36:10.083
You were half-dead
when you left that night.

492
00:36:10.166 --> 00:36:12.166
[both laughing]

493
00:36:13.958 --> 00:36:15.500
[Aureliano II sighs]

494
00:36:18.750 --> 00:36:19.916
[Aureliano II groans]

495
00:36:21.208 --> 00:36:22.541
[Aureliano II sighs]

496
00:36:25.500 --> 00:36:27.000
Heard the big news.

497
00:36:30.083 --> 00:36:31.916
I'm sure you must be happy.

498
00:36:34.916 --> 00:36:37.416
I can't imagine one more day
without seeing you.

499
00:36:37.500 --> 00:36:39.500
[accordion music playing]

500
00:36:40.666 --> 00:36:43.750
But I also can't abandon my unborn child.
or Meme right now.

501
00:36:48.291 --> 00:36:49.333
[Petra chuckles]

502
00:37:01.416 --> 00:37:02.333
[music stops]

503
00:37:04.750 --> 00:37:06.208
[man] You owe us money. We were sick.

504
00:37:06.291 --> 00:37:09.416
[Gavilán] We just wanna talk. Mr. Brown.
We can't do anything!

505
00:37:09.916 --> 00:37:12.416
- We just wanna talk to Mr. Brown.
- [man] He's trying to screw us!

506
00:37:12.500 --> 00:37:14.375
- We wanna speak to him!
- [Gavilán] Get off of me!

507
00:37:14.458 --> 00:37:16.458
[José Arcadio II] Hey. hey!
What the hell's going on?

508
00:37:16.541 --> 00:37:18.291
Yeah! Enough! What is going on?

509
00:37:18.375 --> 00:37:19.750
What do you mean "what's going on"?

510
00:37:19.833 --> 00:37:22.125
They're saying they won't pay us
since we went to a doctor.

511
00:37:22.625 --> 00:37:25.458
[Gavilán] This is messed up. man.
This is abuse of power!

512
00:37:26.291 --> 00:37:27.958
[guard] Yeah. yeah. Keep moving. Let's go.

513
00:37:28.041 --> 00:37:29.833
[man 3] You don't make the law
around here!

514
00:37:29.916 --> 00:37:31.083
[guard] Hey. calm down.

515
00:37:37.791 --> 00:37:39.000
Mr. Buendía!

516
00:37:40.541 --> 00:37:42.541
[José Arcadio II]
Why haven't the workers been paid?

517
00:37:43.083 --> 00:37:44.500
Did you forget to knock?

518
00:37:44.583 --> 00:37:47.166
They went to see a doctor
with your authorization.

519
00:37:51.333 --> 00:37:53.250
And who told them
that they were getting paid

520
00:37:53.333 --> 00:37:55.625
for going to see a doctor. buddy?

521
00:37:55.708 --> 00:37:56.666
[snickers]

522
00:37:58.166 --> 00:38:00.208
Don't act so surprised. all right?

523
00:38:00.291 --> 00:38:02.250
Our company
is not a charitable foundation.

524
00:38:02.333 --> 00:38:04.791
If you don't work. you don't get paid.

525
00:38:06.208 --> 00:38:08.458
Is that why you had them
kicked out of the building?

526
00:38:09.958 --> 00:38:12.375
- All they wanted was to have a word.
- They're not here to talk.

527
00:38:12.458 --> 00:38:14.958
They're here to cut bananas.
for God's sake!

528
00:38:16.333 --> 00:38:18.041
Jesus Christ!

529
00:38:21.125 --> 00:38:22.250
[Mr. Brown sighs]

530
00:38:24.625 --> 00:38:27.500
This is unlike you. José Arcadio Buendía.

531
00:38:31.541 --> 00:38:35.416
Or are you letting them feed your head
with their silly communist ideas?

532
00:38:35.916 --> 00:38:37.083
That it?

533
00:38:37.166 --> 00:38:38.000
Huh?

534
00:38:44.208 --> 00:38:46.666
Just get them under control. foreman.

535
00:38:48.875 --> 00:38:51.083
You don't really want to be against me.

536
00:39:04.750 --> 00:39:06.750
[insects chittering]

537
00:39:14.791 --> 00:39:16.833
[José Arcadio II]
I know this isn't enough.

538
00:39:17.875 --> 00:39:20.541
but the only thing that I can do for now…

539
00:39:22.791 --> 00:39:25.083
is give everyone twice as many vouchers

540
00:39:25.166 --> 00:39:27.750
so you can use them
at the town commissary.

541
00:39:45.125 --> 00:39:47.958
Listen. I know you mean well.
José Arcadio…

542
00:39:49.958 --> 00:39:53.166
but I'm afraid you still have
much to understand in this life

543
00:39:54.958 --> 00:39:58.500
if you really believe that our dignity
is only worth some Virginia ham.

544
00:40:05.791 --> 00:40:06.833
Gavilán.

545
00:40:09.166 --> 00:40:10.458
I'm on your side.

546
00:40:10.541 --> 00:40:12.541
[somber music playing]

547
00:40:13.833 --> 00:40:15.000
Then show us.

548
00:40:36.125 --> 00:40:38.125
[indistinct chattering]

549
00:40:57.833 --> 00:41:00.541
IN MEMORY OF COLONEL AURELIANO BUENDÍA

550
00:41:04.375 --> 00:41:05.791
[music fades]

551
00:41:09.291 --> 00:41:11.291
[melodic music playing]

552
00:41:11.375 --> 00:41:12.833
[indistinct chattering]

553
00:41:12.916 --> 00:41:15.625
THEY LEFT THE DOLL.
IT WAS SO BEAUTIFUL I WANTED TO STEAL IT…

554
00:41:35.291 --> 00:41:36.750
[man] Corn. fresh corn.

555
00:41:42.166 --> 00:41:45.583
[narrator] <i>The first Saturday</i>
<i>she went to the cinema with her father.</i>

556
00:41:45.666 --> 00:41:48.500
<i>Meme saw Mauricio Babilonia again.</i>

557
00:41:51.583 --> 00:41:56.166
<i>And the anxiety was so overwhelming</i>
<i>that she had to make a tremendous effort</i>

558
00:41:56.250 --> 00:41:57.791
<i>to keep anyone from noticing</i>

559
00:41:57.875 --> 00:42:00.750
<i>that her heart was leaping</i>
<i>out of her mouth.</i>

560
00:42:00.833 --> 00:42:02.625
- Poor girl.
- Mm-hmm.

561
00:42:06.041 --> 00:42:08.583
[Aureliano II] What a great movie.
I thought it was beautiful.

562
00:42:08.666 --> 00:42:10.125
[Mauricio] Good evening. Mr. Buendía.

563
00:42:10.208 --> 00:42:12.166
Well. well Mr. Babilonia.

564
00:42:12.250 --> 00:42:15.666
- How's work treating you these days?
- It's nonstop. You know how it is.

565
00:42:15.750 --> 00:42:18.125
At least you make enough money
for a night out like this.

566
00:42:18.208 --> 00:42:20.166
- Hmm.
- Have you met my daughter?

567
00:42:20.791 --> 00:42:21.708
No.

568
00:42:22.666 --> 00:42:24.125
It's nice to meet you. miss.

569
00:42:24.208 --> 00:42:26.208
[mysterious music playing]

570
00:42:31.458 --> 00:42:35.041
[narrator] <i>Bewildered by a strange mixture</i>
<i>of pleasure and rage…</i>

571
00:42:38.666 --> 00:42:40.458
<i>she gave him her hand…</i>

572
00:42:46.791 --> 00:42:50.250
<i>and almost instantly regretted</i>
<i>the impulse.</i>

573
00:42:50.916 --> 00:42:54.875
<i>though the regret</i>
<i>quickly turned into a cruel satisfaction…</i>

574
00:42:55.583 --> 00:42:56.791
It was a pleasure to see you.

575
00:42:56.875 --> 00:42:58.750
- Good night. Babilonia.
- Evening.

576
00:42:59.291 --> 00:43:04.291
<i>…as she realized that his hand. too.</i>
<i>was sweaty and cold as ice.</i>

577
00:43:08.333 --> 00:43:09.541
[music fades]

578
00:43:19.833 --> 00:43:21.833
[Amaranta snoring]

579
00:43:39.083 --> 00:43:41.083
[indistinct chattering]

580
00:43:43.708 --> 00:43:44.916
[car horn honks]

581
00:43:45.791 --> 00:43:47.041
[Patricia] Meme!

582
00:43:48.375 --> 00:43:49.833
[Patricia laughs]

583
00:43:50.708 --> 00:43:53.083
You can't wear that to the party. Meme!

584
00:43:53.166 --> 00:43:55.250
[both laugh]

585
00:43:55.333 --> 00:43:56.250
Catch!

586
00:43:57.791 --> 00:43:58.625
Ready?

587
00:43:59.375 --> 00:44:01.375
[both laughing]

588
00:44:02.916 --> 00:44:05.416
[Patricia] Get out of here! Whoo!

589
00:44:07.125 --> 00:44:09.166
- It's pretty. right?
- [young Meme] So pretty!

590
00:44:09.250 --> 00:44:11.250
[percussive music playing]

591
00:44:17.625 --> 00:44:18.666
[music stops]

592
00:44:19.583 --> 00:44:21.750
[man] One. two… A one. two. three. four!

593
00:44:21.833 --> 00:44:24.083
- [crowd whooping]
- [lively jazz music playing]

594
00:44:44.750 --> 00:44:45.708
[gasps]

595
00:44:52.708 --> 00:44:53.916
You're amazing!

596
00:44:54.000 --> 00:44:56.000
[music continues in distance]

597
00:45:14.750 --> 00:45:16.416
Re… Renata.

598
00:45:44.125 --> 00:45:46.166
[screams. laughs]

599
00:45:46.250 --> 00:45:47.291
[gasps]

600
00:45:47.375 --> 00:45:49.375
[mysterious music playing]

601
00:45:56.625 --> 00:45:58.625
[lively jazz music resumes]

602
00:46:11.500 --> 00:46:12.458
Whoa!

603
00:46:18.875 --> 00:46:20.958
[lively jazz music continues in distance]

604
00:46:26.666 --> 00:46:28.875
[panting]

605
00:46:31.583 --> 00:46:32.458
[gasps]

606
00:46:32.541 --> 00:46:33.666
[music stops]

607
00:46:34.208 --> 00:46:36.208
[breathing heavily]

608
00:46:56.291 --> 00:46:58.291
[clattering]

609
00:47:04.083 --> 00:47:05.208
[young Meme] Hello.

610
00:47:08.416 --> 00:47:09.291
Hey.

611
00:47:10.791 --> 00:47:14.208
Patricia said you got new cars.
and. um. I…

612
00:47:14.291 --> 00:47:15.625
Well. I wanted to see 'em.

613
00:47:20.000 --> 00:47:21.541
That's some story.

614
00:47:26.750 --> 00:47:27.875
But don't worry.

615
00:47:30.541 --> 00:47:33.458
It's not the first time
a woman's gone crazy for a man.

616
00:47:36.458 --> 00:47:38.583
Don't be ridiculous. Babilonia.

617
00:47:40.291 --> 00:47:44.125
A guy like you would be lucky
to have a woman like me.

618
00:47:44.625 --> 00:47:46.625
[intriguing music playing]

619
00:47:47.250 --> 00:47:48.166
[young Meme gasps]

620
00:47:48.250 --> 00:47:50.375
[narrator] <i>The first time they were alone.</i>

621
00:47:51.083 --> 00:47:54.166
<i>he mercilessly dragged her</i>
<i>into an animalistic state</i>

622
00:47:54.250 --> 00:47:55.833
<i>that left her exhausted.</i>

623
00:47:56.541 --> 00:47:58.541
[moaning]

624
00:47:59.250 --> 00:48:04.083
<i>It took Meme some time to understand</i>
<i>that this. too. was a form of tenderness.</i>

625
00:48:06.541 --> 00:48:09.083
<i>It was then when she lost her composure.</i>

626
00:48:10.625 --> 00:48:11.625
Let me go.

627
00:48:11.708 --> 00:48:12.625
[music stops]

628
00:48:16.041 --> 00:48:17.291
[Mauricio chuckles]

629
00:48:39.916 --> 00:48:40.958
[sighs]

630
00:48:46.250 --> 00:48:47.125
[chuckles]

631
00:48:47.625 --> 00:48:50.250
- [lively music playing]
- [man] Come on. Let's go. Let's play.

632
00:48:50.333 --> 00:48:51.333
Let's play.

633
00:48:51.416 --> 00:48:53.416
[fireworks exploding]

634
00:48:55.625 --> 00:48:58.291
[man] Bring that bottle over here.
Are you finishing it on your own?

635
00:48:58.958 --> 00:49:00.833
[indistinct chattering]

636
00:49:13.375 --> 00:49:15.375
[lively music continues]

637
00:49:24.458 --> 00:49:26.541
You are Aureliano's daughter.

638
00:49:27.333 --> 00:49:29.833
I recognize a Buendía a mile away.

639
00:49:29.916 --> 00:49:32.000
Especially when they're deep in love.

640
00:49:33.208 --> 00:49:36.000
You don't have anyone
to talk to about it. do you?

641
00:49:36.083 --> 00:49:38.583
You're welcome to come over anytime.

642
00:49:38.666 --> 00:49:41.916
When you're ready.
just ask anyone where Pilar lives.

643
00:49:42.000 --> 00:49:43.083
Everyone here knows.

644
00:49:43.166 --> 00:49:44.875
I'll be waiting for you.

645
00:49:44.958 --> 00:49:46.958
[lively music continues]

646
00:50:11.875 --> 00:50:12.875
[Aureliano II] Meme!

647
00:50:13.875 --> 00:50:15.125
[both] Let me explain.

648
00:50:18.041 --> 00:50:19.541
[Aureliano II laughs]

649
00:50:19.625 --> 00:50:21.625
[both laughing]

650
00:50:31.750 --> 00:50:34.458
So I'm guessing she's why you and Mom
are always fighting.

651
00:50:39.333 --> 00:50:40.250
Petra.

652
00:50:40.833 --> 00:50:41.666
Meme.

653
00:50:44.708 --> 00:50:45.583
Nice to meet you.

654
00:50:46.500 --> 00:50:47.583
Yeah. you too.

655
00:50:52.125 --> 00:50:52.958
No.

656
00:50:54.708 --> 00:50:56.708
[both laughing]

657
00:50:57.833 --> 00:50:59.833
[lively music continues in distance]

658
00:51:00.750 --> 00:51:02.916
[Aureliano II]
Love is complicated. sweetheart.

659
00:51:03.000 --> 00:51:04.916
[fireworks explode in distance]

660
00:51:05.625 --> 00:51:08.375
I swear no one will ever find out
you were here tonight.

661
00:51:08.458 --> 00:51:11.750
but you have to promise to tell me
when you fall in love with someone.

662
00:51:15.708 --> 00:51:17.833
But how do you know
when you've fallen in love?

663
00:51:18.916 --> 00:51:21.625
Oh. that's easy.
You feel like the earth is shaking.

664
00:51:28.875 --> 00:51:29.958
Promise me.

665
00:51:45.333 --> 00:51:46.375
[knocking at door]

666
00:51:46.458 --> 00:51:48.250
Wait. careful. Meme.

667
00:51:48.333 --> 00:51:50.000
Careful you don't prick yourself.

668
00:51:50.083 --> 00:51:51.458
[both laugh]

669
00:51:51.541 --> 00:51:54.041
- [Sofía] Good morning.
- [Mauricio] Good morning.

670
00:51:54.125 --> 00:51:55.666
[Sofía] What can I do for you?

671
00:51:55.750 --> 00:51:58.250
[Mauricio] This is a gift
from Miss Patricia Brown to Miss Renata.

672
00:51:58.333 --> 00:52:00.916
Look at how beautifully
these have bloomed.

673
00:52:01.000 --> 00:52:03.416
- [Sofía] You have a good day now.
- [Mauricio] Thank you.

674
00:52:04.750 --> 00:52:06.666
[Sofía] Hmm. never seen him before.

675
00:52:06.750 --> 00:52:08.750
[intriguing music playing]

676
00:52:08.833 --> 00:52:09.833
[Sofía] Meme.

677
00:52:11.916 --> 00:52:12.750
Here.

678
00:52:13.375 --> 00:52:14.833
Someone sent this.

679
00:52:16.000 --> 00:52:17.791
What's gotten into you?

680
00:52:17.875 --> 00:52:20.000
[Úrsula] She is her father's daughter.

681
00:52:20.583 --> 00:52:21.791
[chuckles]

682
00:52:27.041 --> 00:52:28.208
Renata. what are you…

683
00:52:35.833 --> 00:52:37.958
[panting]

684
00:52:56.500 --> 00:52:57.625
[chuckles]

685
00:53:04.375 --> 00:53:06.375
- [music stops]
- [machete slices]

686
00:53:07.291 --> 00:53:09.208
[man 1] Hey. Juan.
hand me the ladder. will you?

687
00:53:11.166 --> 00:53:12.708
[indistinct chattering]

688
00:53:12.791 --> 00:53:15.125
[man 2] You get that side.
I'll get the other.

689
00:53:15.208 --> 00:53:17.208
[ominous music playing]

690
00:53:26.708 --> 00:53:28.708
[car horn honks]

691
00:53:30.708 --> 00:53:32.708
[indistinct shouting]

692
00:53:36.250 --> 00:53:38.000
[music fades]

693
00:53:39.333 --> 00:53:40.250
Everything all right?

694
00:53:40.333 --> 00:53:42.500
You tell me. Is everything all right here?

695
00:53:43.791 --> 00:53:45.125
It sure is. yeah.

696
00:53:49.625 --> 00:53:51.625
[mysterious music playing]

697
00:53:56.625 --> 00:54:02.041
TOMORROW AT 7 PM AT THE MATRON'S PLACE

698
00:54:09.708 --> 00:54:11.041
[music fades]

699
00:54:11.125 --> 00:54:12.041
Here.

700
00:54:12.958 --> 00:54:14.458
- This will do you well.
- Mm.

701
00:54:14.541 --> 00:54:15.708
[Úrsula chuckles]

702
00:54:16.250 --> 00:54:17.125
Thanks.

703
00:54:20.208 --> 00:54:21.208
Renata.

704
00:54:22.708 --> 00:54:24.500
I'm still waiting for an apology.

705
00:54:25.541 --> 00:54:27.208
I don't feel that well. Mama.

706
00:54:36.583 --> 00:54:39.375
[Úrsula] Fernanda.
this is not just about Meme.

707
00:54:40.750 --> 00:54:43.291
There comes a day in every mother's life

708
00:54:45.375 --> 00:54:48.916
when we realize there's no way for us
to control our children.

709
00:54:50.500 --> 00:54:54.791
Don't take this the wrong way
'cause I only say this with love.

710
00:54:55.416 --> 00:54:57.875
The more that you try
to change your daughter.

711
00:54:58.875 --> 00:55:00.333
the farther she will drift away.

712
00:55:01.791 --> 00:55:04.000
Here. Put those on the table.

713
00:55:06.333 --> 00:55:08.333
[indistinct chattering]

714
00:55:09.958 --> 00:55:13.083
Hey. do me a favor.
Tell me where I can find Pilar Ternera.

715
00:55:13.166 --> 00:55:14.833
Sure. that red house over there.

716
00:55:15.333 --> 00:55:16.208
Thanks.

717
00:55:38.458 --> 00:55:41.416
I don't need to read your cards
to know what's going on.

718
00:55:41.958 --> 00:55:45.000
You have the same look
the colonel had when he confessed to me

719
00:55:45.083 --> 00:55:47.833
that he'd fallen in love
with the wrong person.

720
00:55:50.916 --> 00:55:52.583
Do you believe it's worth the risk?

721
00:55:53.083 --> 00:55:55.208
True love is always worth it.

722
00:55:56.125 --> 00:56:01.000
But the issue is you must try first
to know if it is true or not.

723
00:56:01.083 --> 00:56:03.083
[suspenseful music playing]

724
00:56:11.166 --> 00:56:12.208
Come on.

725
00:56:18.875 --> 00:56:22.000
[narrator] <i>Pilar Ternera</i>
<i>not only dispelled her fears.</i>

726
00:56:23.708 --> 00:56:26.083
<i>but also offered Meme the old canvas bed</i>

727
00:56:26.166 --> 00:56:29.583
<i>where she conceived Arcadio.</i>
<i>Meme's grandfather.</i>

728
00:56:29.666 --> 00:56:32.666
<i>and where she later conceived</i>
<i>Aureliano José.</i>

729
00:56:34.000 --> 00:56:35.083
[Mauricio] Give me two.

730
00:56:35.166 --> 00:56:37.166
[lively jazz music playing]

731
00:56:39.500 --> 00:56:40.333
Thanks.

732
00:56:42.625 --> 00:56:45.250
[man] Next? How many tickets do you want?

733
00:56:54.416 --> 00:56:55.583
[Pilar] Babilonia?

734
00:56:56.541 --> 00:56:58.333
Mauricio Babilonia?

735
00:56:58.833 --> 00:57:00.333
- Yes.
- Come on.

736
00:57:00.416 --> 00:57:01.791
Come with me.

737
00:57:01.875 --> 00:57:04.958
Trust me. It is in your best interest.

738
00:57:11.916 --> 00:57:13.708
[poignant music playing]

739
00:58:11.750 --> 00:58:13.208
[Renata breathes shakily]

740
00:58:28.083 --> 00:58:30.083
[melancholy French music playing]

741
00:58:50.708 --> 00:58:53.000
[woman moaning]

742
00:58:58.375 --> 00:58:59.708
[moaning continues]

743
00:59:11.458 --> 00:59:13.875
One complaint from us.
one single complaint.

744
00:59:15.041 --> 00:59:18.000
and now we've got guards watching us
every time we take a piss.

745
00:59:20.916 --> 00:59:24.250
Why do we have to hide and sneak around
like we're a bunch of criminals?

746
00:59:26.125 --> 00:59:28.625
I helped establish this thing.
José Arcadio.

747
00:59:28.708 --> 00:59:30.375
but this is messed up. all right?

748
00:59:31.083 --> 00:59:33.125
They just keep asking for more.

749
00:59:33.208 --> 00:59:35.208
I'll fund something else
if things don't change.

750
00:59:35.291 --> 00:59:36.500
Yeah. me too.

751
00:59:36.583 --> 00:59:38.375
Even if I have to leave Macondo.

752
00:59:38.875 --> 00:59:40.416
This can't go on any longer.

753
00:59:40.916 --> 00:59:42.583
And it shouldn't have to either.

754
00:59:43.083 --> 00:59:44.833
[Gavilán]So how long do we put up with it?

755
00:59:47.000 --> 00:59:47.833
Huh?

756
00:59:49.500 --> 00:59:51.958
How much longer until we can show
these motherfucking gringos

757
00:59:52.041 --> 00:59:53.375
that. without us.

758
00:59:54.333 --> 00:59:55.708
they have nothing?

759
00:59:56.375 --> 01:00:00.958
Listen. Buendía. We're moving forward
on our own. with or without you.

760
01:00:01.041 --> 01:00:02.791
We need to know whose side you're on.

761
01:00:04.041 --> 01:00:05.250
Yeah. he's right.

762
01:00:06.458 --> 01:00:08.041
You need to think about it. boss.

763
01:00:18.000 --> 01:00:19.000
[music stops]

764
01:00:32.750 --> 01:00:33.791
Renata.

765
01:00:44.041 --> 01:00:45.041
Renata?

766
01:00:45.541 --> 01:00:46.583
Are you all right?

767
01:00:54.708 --> 01:00:56.708
[tense music playing]

768
01:00:57.583 --> 01:01:00.000
[breathing shakily]

769
01:01:04.958 --> 01:01:07.416
- [young Meme laughs]
- Come on. slowpoke. faster!

770
01:01:07.500 --> 01:01:08.958
Faster. huh?

771
01:01:09.041 --> 01:01:10.833
[both laughing]

772
01:01:11.958 --> 01:01:13.125
Keep up! [laughs]

773
01:01:13.208 --> 01:01:14.833
[young Meme laughing]

774
01:01:16.333 --> 01:01:17.458
I'm gonna beat you!

775
01:01:17.541 --> 01:01:18.916
[Mauricio screams. laughs]

776
01:01:19.000 --> 01:01:21.333
[indistinct chattering]

777
01:01:21.416 --> 01:01:23.166
Thank you for coming. José Arcadio.

778
01:01:23.875 --> 01:01:25.833
Take care. all right? And think about it.

779
01:01:25.916 --> 01:01:26.750
Yes.

780
01:01:29.083 --> 01:01:30.166
See you later.

781
01:01:31.666 --> 01:01:33.083
- See you.
- Thanks. man.

782
01:01:33.583 --> 01:01:34.708
Good luck. foreman.

783
01:01:35.625 --> 01:01:37.625
[tense music continues]

784
01:02:04.333 --> 01:02:06.250
Where are you off to. sister?

785
01:02:06.333 --> 01:02:08.333
[melodic acoustic guitar music playing]

786
01:02:36.916 --> 01:02:38.916
[tense music playing]

787
01:02:40.333 --> 01:02:42.333
[laughter]

788
01:02:57.625 --> 01:02:59.625
[lively music playing]

789
01:03:06.625 --> 01:03:08.625
[dark ethereal music playing]

790
01:03:11.291 --> 01:03:13.916
[narrator] <i>From the shadows</i>
<i>of the box seats.</i>

791
01:03:14.000 --> 01:03:16.458
<i>Fernanda recognized her daughter.</i>

792
01:03:19.291 --> 01:03:21.291
[dark ethereal music continues]

793
01:03:26.875 --> 01:03:28.083
[man 1] So what do you think?

794
01:03:29.916 --> 01:03:32.083
[Gavilán] I don't think
we can count on him right now.

795
01:03:32.791 --> 01:03:34.500
but we can't wait for him either.

796
01:03:45.000 --> 01:03:46.375
Come on. boys. let's g--

797
01:03:56.583 --> 01:03:57.416
Renata.

798
01:03:57.500 --> 01:04:00.458
[narrator] <i>Although the satisfaction</i>
<i>she got from being right</i>

799
01:04:00.541 --> 01:04:03.458
<i>prevented her from seeing the man</i>
<i>her daughter was kissing.</i>

800
01:04:03.541 --> 01:04:06.875
<i>amid the jeering.</i>
<i>Fernanda caught the tremor in his voice.</i>

801
01:04:06.958 --> 01:04:08.250
[Mauricio] I'm sorry. my love.

802
01:04:08.333 --> 01:04:10.333
[audience whistling. shouting]

803
01:04:14.625 --> 01:04:15.708
[young Meme gasps]

804
01:04:15.791 --> 01:04:17.791
[dark ethereal music continues]

805
01:04:18.958 --> 01:04:20.958
[people murmuring]

806
01:04:25.750 --> 01:04:28.541
[grunting]

807
01:04:45.041 --> 01:04:47.041
[train tracks rattling]

808
01:04:57.208 --> 01:04:59.208
[music fades]

809
01:05:06.833 --> 01:05:09.041
[somber music playing]

810
01:06:53.250 --> 01:06:55.250
[music fades]

811
01:07:01.166 --> 01:07:03.166
[mysterious ethereal music playing]

812
01:13:31.583 --> 01:13:34.625
[music fades]
